test_dfn -- del_vor on fracture networks (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_dfn_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]   3 runs, about 2 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  A fracture network: triangles in several planes, one itetclr per
  fracture, crossing along shared edges (an intersection edge is in 2
  triangles of each fracture it belongs to). del_vor pairs each edge
  with the triangle of the same fracture, checks orientation and the
  Delaunay property fracture by fracture, and adds every fracture's
  share into one coefficient per vertex pair.

  dfn3        made by make_dfn_inputs.py: 3 fractures, 1406
              triangles. Fractures 1 (z = 0.5) and 2 (x = 0.5) cross
              along 16 intersection edges; fracture 3 is tilted and
              meets nothing. Each fracture is triangulated with exact
              Bowyer-Watson, so it is exactly Delaunay.
  dfn3_flip   the same with one triangle of fracture 2 turned over
  full_mesh   Carl's 4-fracture dfnWorks example 4_user_rects_uniform,
              the design's mesh (inputs/, 771 vertices, 1386
              triangles; no parent/child vertices)

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_dfn.py; tolerance 2e-14, relative)

  counts        interior and boundary edges, ties, violations and
                intersection edges equal the exact numbers
                (../exact_check.py)
  coefficients  every A/d in the .stor equals the cotangent formula,
                sum of cot(opposite angle) / 2 over every triangle
                holding the edge, all fractures together
  areas         every control area equals the Voronoi share of the
                vertex, triangle by triangle; they add up to the
                fractures' area
  digits        every real in the .stor and .uge has 17 significant
                digits; the .uge volumes equal the .stor volumes
  orientation   no orientation error (dfn3); for dfn3_flip: exit 1,
                the orientation error naming the turned-over triangle,
                no .stor
  full_mesh     also the sizes: 771 vertices, 1386 triangles, 4
                fractures, 60 intersection, 1942 interior, 274
                boundary edges

PICTURES (logs/)

  NAME.svg  an iso view: each fracture in its own color, the
            intersection edges black, the triangle a message names red

FILES

  run_dfn_tests.sh     runner (work/, logs/)
  make_dfn_inputs.py   dfn3.inp, dfn3_flip.inp
  check_dfn.py         checks, pictures, summary.html
  cases.txt            name | mesh | arguments | what it does
  inputs/README        where Carl's example goes
